# Local vault configuration and derived indexes must never be committed.
.recallweave/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
index-output/
local-config.json
private/
REVIEW-*.md
REMEDIATION-*.md

# Graph exports describe a real vault. Even the default structure-only profile
# carries relative paths, titles, tags, status, domains, citations, and
# note-derived candidate terms -- see viewer/README.md. `recallweave
# export-viewer` documents `recallweave-graph.json` as its output name, so the
# documented happy path would otherwise leave a real graph committable in the
# repository root, and viewer/public/ is where one would naturally be dropped to
# preview it locally.
#
# The bundled synthetic fixture is the only graph that belongs in this repo.
# Prefer exporting to a path OUTSIDE this working tree; graph-exports/ exists as
# a local convenience for when that is impractical.
/recallweave-graph.json
*-graph.json
!viewer/public/sample-graph.json
graph-exports/

# Editors and operating systems.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Beads / Dolt issue tracker — internal development infrastructure, not part of
# the public OSS product. The live database and its passive JSONL exports are
# not tracked in this repo; public issue tracking is GitHub Issues.
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key
/.beads/

# bv (beads viewer) local config and caches
.bv/

# NTM creates per-agent git worktrees and OpenCode lane state under .ntm/ inside
# the project directory. Those are local orchestration artifacts, not source.
.ntm/

# Local Codex review output — generated development artifacts, not source.
.codex-reviews/

# Internal development infrastructure kept out of the public OSS tree: private
# orchestration doctrine, session/planner handoffs, and the local AI-agent tool
# configuration tied to the internal Beads workflow. These describe how one
# maintainer runs a private multi-agent dev swarm and are not needed to build,
# test, or use RecallWeave.
SWARM-RUNBOOK.md
docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md
/.claude/
/.codex/
/.agents/

# Local checkpoint-authorization state written by the private supervisor's push
# gate. It is machine-local supervisor state and must never be tracked or reach
# origin. (The gate reads it from a gitignored path; see the supervisor's
# ensure_checkpoint_marker.) The bare root filename is also ignored so the older
# tracked-marker location can never be recreated as a tracked file.
/.rw-supervisor/
/CHECKPOINT_NOT_APPROVED.md

# Local uv lockfile (project uses pip/setuptools packaging)
uv.lock
